---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import ButtonLink from '../components/ButtonLink.astro';
import { contact } from '../data/contact';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Meet Evan Lebrecht and learn how independent thinking, plain communication, and practical problem-solving shape Calypso Digital Studio."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="About the studio"
    title="I build by asking better questions, not by forcing businesses into a template."
    description="Calypso Digital Studio combines thoughtful design, practical development, and a direct working relationship with the person building your project."
  />

  <section class="about container">
    <div class="about__story">
      <p class="eyebrow">The person behind the work</p>
      <h2>Practical problem-solving, shaped by real-world experience.</h2>
      <p>
        I’m Evan Lebrecht, the designer and developer behind Calypso Digital Studio.
        Before turning this work into a business, I built experience through
        customer-facing jobs, team leadership, community advocacy, political
        organizing, and independent software projects.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those experiences taught me how to listen closely, explain complicated
        issues in plain language, defend an idea with evidence, and keep moving
        when time, money, or resources are limited.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have never been interested in accepting a system simply because
        “that’s how it works.” I look at who it serves, where it breaks down,
        what incentives shape it, and what would make it more useful to the
        people relying on it. That same mindset guides every website and custom
        tool I build.
      </p>
      <p>
        The studio is based in New York’s Capital Region and works with clients
        anywhere.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="about__brand surface">
      <img
        src="/assets/brand/calypso-master.webp"
        alt="Calypso Digital Studio illustrated logo"
        width="1200"
        height="1200"
      />
      <figcaption>
        The studio is named after Calypso. Her markings and personality shaped
        the warm, organic identity without turning the business into a novelty brand.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="mindset container">
    <header class="mindset__intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">How I approach the work</p>
      <h2>The goal is not to sell the most features. It is to build the right system.</h2>
      <p>
        I care about what a project accomplishes in real use: what customers
        understand, what the owner can manage, what slows the business down, and
        what will still make sense after launch.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mindset__grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Independent thinking</h3>
        <p>
          Recommendations come from the business, its customers, and the evidence—not
          from a trend, a template, or a platform I am trying to sell.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Plain language</h3>
        <p>
          Clients should be able to understand what is being built, why it matters,
          and what decisions still need to be made.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Real-world usefulness</h3>
        <p>
          Pages and features should solve an actual problem, improve a workflow,
          or help a customer take the next step.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Honest accountability</h3>
        <p>
          Scope, limitations, progress, recommendations, and project status should
          be clear—even when the honest answer is that something is unnecessary.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="contact-card container surface">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact Evan</p>
      <h2>Have a business problem that may need a website or custom tool?</h2>
      <p>
        Email is the most direct way to begin. You can also see more of my work,
        interests, and public-facing background through the studio’s social profiles.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="contact-card__links">
      <a class="contact-card__email" href={contact.emailHref}>{contact.email}</a>
      <a href={contact.instagram.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        {contact.instagram.label}
      </a>
      <a href={contact.facebook.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        {contact.facebook.label}
      </a>
      <ButtonLink href="/start">Start Your Project</ButtonLink>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .about__story p:not(.eyebrow) {
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .about__brand {
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .about__brand figcaption {
    padding: var(--space-4);
  }

  .mindset {
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
  }

  .mindset__intro {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .mindset__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .mindset__grid article {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }

  .contact-card {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-block: var(--space-7);
    padding: var(--space-6);
  }

  .contact-card__links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .contact-card__links > a:not(.button) {
    font-weight: 800;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-rust);
    text-decoration-thickness: 0.12em;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .contact-card__email {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .mindset__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.75fr;
    }

    .contact-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
      padding: var(--space-7);
    }
  }
</style>
